# Deep-Guard Fix — 2026-07-10T20:06:09+03:30
# File: /tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js  Line: 235  Severity: critical
# Type: path_traversal

## Root Cause
External entity processing is enabled, allowing for path traversal attacks via XML.

## Explanation
The patch sets the 'noent' option to false in the parseXmlString function. This prevents external entities from being processed, which mitigates the risk of path traversal vulnerabilities by ensuring that any malicious XML content cannot access the filesystem.

## Patch
--- a/tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js
+++ b/tmp/dvna/core/appHandler.js
@@ -235 +235 @@
-        var products = libxmljs.parseXmlString(req.files.products.data.toString('utf8'), {noent:true,noblanks:true})
+        var products = libxmljs.parseXmlString(req.files.products.data.toString('utf8'), {noent:false,noblanks:true})
